---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SignIcon from '../../../components/SignIcon.astro';
import { SIGNS } from '../../../lib/signs';
import { EDITOR_AUTHOR } from '../../../lib/editorial';

const PAGE_URL = 'https://zodiacs.org/learn/communication/';
const PAGE_DATE = '2026-07-14';
const title = 'Communication Styles by Birth Chart: Mercury, Moon & Mars | Zodiacs.org';
const description = 'How you think, what a conversation needs to feel like, and how you handle friction, read from Mercury, the Moon, and Mars in your birth chart.';
const headline = 'How your chart talks';
const sources = [
  { label: 'Calculation methodology', href: 'https://zodiacs.org/methodology/' },
];
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@type': 'Article',
    '@id': `${PAGE_URL}#article`,
    headline,
    description,
    url: PAGE_URL,
    datePublished: PAGE_DATE,
    dateModified: PAGE_DATE,
    author: EDITOR_AUTHOR,
    publisher: { '@id': 'https://zodiacs.org/#org' },
    mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': PAGE_URL },
    inLanguage: 'en',
    isAccessibleForFree: true,
    citation: sources.map((source) => ({
      '@type': 'CreativeWork',
      name: source.label,
      url: source.href,
    })),
  },
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Zodiacs.org', item: 'https://zodiacs.org/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Learn', item: 'https://zodiacs.org/learn/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Communication', item: PAGE_URL },
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/learn/communication/"
  type="article"
  image="/assets/og/v2/tool/learn.png"
  imageAlt="How your chart talks, Zodiacs.org"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  sources={sources}
>
  <article class="communication container container--narrow">
    <header class="communication__hero reveal">
      <h1 class="display">How your chart talks</h1>
      <p class="communication__lede">Sun-sign lists will tell you how to text a Taurus. Your chart can do better: Mercury shows how you actually think and phrase things, the Moon shows what a conversation has to feel like before you'll stay in it, and Mars shows what happens when it turns into a disagreement. All three are computed here, on your device, from your real birth data.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="communication__sections reveal">
      <section>
        <h2>Mercury: the voice</h2>
        <p>Mercury's sign is the register your thinking runs in: fast or deliberate, literal or lateral, blunt or diplomatic. It's the difference between people who think by talking and people who talk once the thinking is done. Find yours below, or compute the whole chart and read it in place.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>The Moon: the listener</h2>
        <p>The Moon doesn't speak; it decides whether the room feels safe enough to keep speaking. Two people with easy Mercury contact can still talk past each other if one Moon needs the feeling named and the other needs it handled. That's not a communication-skills problem; it's a placement difference, and knowing it changes how you argue.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Mars: the argument</h2>
        <p>Every exchange eventually hits friction, and Mars is the shape yours takes: the flare that's gone by dinner, the cold strategy, the retreat that comes back sideways. None of these styles is wrong. Unnamed, each one convinces the other person it's personal.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="communication__placements reveal" aria-labelledby="mercury-signs">
      <h2 id="mercury-signs">Mercury in every sign</h2>
      <div class="communication__chips">
        {SIGNS.map((sign) => (
          <a
            class="communication__chip"
            href={`/learn/placements/mercury-in-${sign.slug}/`}
            style={`--sign:${sign.hue}`}
          >
            <SignIcon sign={sign.slug} size={16} /> {sign.name}
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="communication__cta reveal">
      <a href="/birth-chart/">Read yours in your chart →</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
      <a href="/compatibility/">See how two charts talk to each other →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .communication {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(30px, 5vw, 48px);
    padding-block: clamp(28px, 5vw, 58px) clamp(42px, 7vw, 80px);
  }
  .communication__hero { display: grid; gap: 14px; max-width: 66ch; }
  .communication__hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.35rem, 1.65rem + 3.4vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .communication__lede {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.65;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .communication__sections {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(24px, 4vw, 36px);
  }
  .communication__sections section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 9px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair-1);
  }
  .communication__sections h2,
  .communication__placements h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .communication__sections p {
    max-width: 66ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .communication__placements { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .communication__chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 2px; }
  .communication__chip {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 4px 10px 4px 5px;
    border-radius: var(--r-full);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color var(--dur-1) var(--ease), background var(--dur-1) var(--ease);
  }
  .communication__chip:hover {
    color: var(--text);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sign) 12%, transparent);
  }
  .communication__chip :global(img) { border-radius: 50%; }
  .communication__cta {
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair-1);
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .communication__cta a { color: var(--text); }
</style>
